    "html": "<p>The board is an infinite surface. Drag on empty space to pan; scroll or pinch to zoom; the zoom\ncontrol and &quot;fit&quot; sit in the corner beside the purpose control.</p>\n<p>A press does different things depending on what it lands on and which modifier is held. On a card\nit selects and opens the focus; on empty space it clears the selection and starts a marquee. With\nShift it adds to the selection. With Alt it does the gesture the current tool names — a link, a\nthread, a web, a pattern — and a click during that modifier commits it rather than previewing.</p>\n<p>Cards stay where you put them. Position is part of the document, so a card moved on this board is\nmoved for everyone on it, and a card can appear on several boards at once. Nothing about the\ncamera is shared: zooming out to see the whole board does not move anyone else&#39;s view.</p>\n<p>The board is also a document, not a page. Every edit is a CRDT operation, which is why two people\ncan type in different cards at the same time and why the canvas keeps working offline.</p>\n",
