    "section": "getting-around",
    "order": 20,
    "targets": [],
    "html": "<p>A press on a card selects it. A press on empty space clears the selection and starts a marquee; drag\naround what you want and release. Shift adds to the selection, or removes from it if the thing is\nalready in. <code>Shift</code> and the arrows extend, <code>Cmd-A</code> or <code>Ctrl-A</code> selects everything on the board, and\nEscape clears.</p>\n<p>The selection is UI state, not document state. It is not synced, it disappears when you leave the\nboard, and it is what several things read: the inspector, the outline, the commands that act on\n&quot;what is selected&quot;, and explain mode.</p>\n<p>A multi-selection intersects rather than unions. Selecting a card and a section shows the tabs both\nhave, so a panel never offers a row that would write to only half of what you picked. Verbs that\ncount say the count — <em>Duplicate 4 cards</em> — because a plural is the only honest way to describe an\noperation on a set.</p>\n<p>Selection also decides what a modifier click does. With Alt held, the current gesture claims the\nclick; without it, a modifier click belongs to selection and never opens the inspector.</p>\n",
