    "html": "<p>The theme control switches between light, dark and system. System follows the device and keeps\nfollowing it, so a laptop that dims at night changes the app without anyone touching this control.</p>\n<p>Everything past the theme lives in <strong>Settings</strong>, which the same menu opens:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Density</strong> — compact reduces the padding inside a card body, so more cards fit on one screen.</li>\n<li><strong>Canvas</strong> — plain hides the dot grid.</li>\n<li><strong>Card radius</strong> — one variable, and a card&#39;s own stored radius still wins.</li>\n<li><strong>Motion</strong> — a preference the interface honours rather than a switch that only its own animations\nread.</li>\n<li><strong>The workspace palette</strong> — the swatches everything else chooses from. This one is document data,\nso it is shared; the rest is this device.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>None of the device settings sync, by design: they change how this screen draws, never what a peer\nsees.</p>\n",
